AIM

To capture and analyze live network traffic using the Wireshark packet analyser and to study the structure of protocol headers at various layers of the TCP/IP stack.

ALGORITHM
v
1. Install and open Wireshark on the system.

2. Select the active network interface (e.g., Wi-Fi/Ethernet) and start a live packet capture.

3. Generate network traffic by opening a website, pinging a host, or running the Java client-server programs from Experiments 1 and 2.


4.Apply display filters such as http, dns, tcp, icmp to isolate the traffic of interest.

5. Select an individual packet and expand the Frame, Ethernet II, Internet Protocol, and Transmission Control Protocol / User Datagram Protocol sections in the packet-details pane.

6. Note down key header fields for each layer: source/destination MAC address, source/destination IP address, TTL, source/destination port numbers, sequence and acknowledgement numbers, and flags (SYN, ACK, FIN).

7. Use Statistics→ Protocol Hierarchy and Follow→ TCP Stream to study the overall traffic composition and reconstruct an application-layer conversation.

8.Stop the capture and save it as a pcapng file for the report.

