# Commands / filters used inside Wireshark

1. Capture filter (before starting capture):

host 192.168.1.10 and port 80 -> web traffic of the host
host 192.168.1.10 and tcp port 5000 -> Echo server traffic (Experiment 1)

2. Display filters (after capture):

http  -> show only HTTP packets
dns -> show only DNS query/response packets
tcp.port == 5000 -> show traffic on the Echo server port
tcp.flags.syn == 1 -> show only TCP SYN (connection setup) packets
icmp-> show ping (ICMP) traffic

3. Menu operations:

Statistics > Protocol Hierarchy
Statistics > Conversations
Right-click packet > Follow > TCP Stream
